llère, applying them to his own serene landscapes of the Seine's environs."},{"source":"work_aw10","target":"work_aw44","type":"work_work","relation_type":"influenced","relation_note":"While stylistically distinct (Pointillism vs. Impressionism), Seurat's monumental depiction of Parisian leisure on the banks of the Seine is a thematic descendant of Monet's earlier, more spontaneous scenes of modern life."},{"source":"work_aw10","target":"work_aw22","type":"work_work","relation_type":"inspired_by","relation_note":"Monet's mentor, Boudin, taught him the value of painting outdoors ('en plein air') and capturing atmospheric effects, a direct methodological precursor to La Grenouillère."},{"source":"work_aw10","target":"work_aw23","type":"work_work","relation_type":"inspired_by","relation_note":"Like many Impressionists, Monet was influenced by Japanese ukiyo-e prints. The asymmetrical compositions, cropped views, and flattened perspectives of artists like Hokusai offered a new visual language visible in the framing of this scene."},{"source":"work_aw10","target":"work_aw42","type":"work_work","relation_type":"inspired_by","relation_note":"Manet's groundbreaking depiction of modern urban leisure provided a crucial precedent for the Impressionists' focus on contemporary social life, moving away from historical or mythological subjects."},{"source":"person_ap6","target":"person_ap64","type":"person_person","relation_type":"influenced_by","relation_note":"Derived: Water Lilies (Grandes Decorations) → On the Beach at Trouville","confidence":"corroborated"},{"source":"person_ap6","target":"person_ap74","type":"person_person","relation_type":"influenced_by","relation_note":"Derived: Water Lilies → The Great Wave off Kanagawa","confidence":"corroborated"},{"source":"person_ap71","target":"person_ap6","type":"person_person","relation_type":"influenced_by","relation_note":"Derived: Impression, Sunrise → The Starry Night","confidence":"corroborated"},{"source":"person_ap67","targe